# Agreement Duration and Transition Dates

This scope calculates key temporal milestones, including the transition period for personnel coverage, the notice period for termination, and the overall duration of the agreement.

```catala
declaration scope AgreementTimeline:
  input end_date_planning_team content date   # End date of the first agreement (31 December 2002)
  input start_date_eu_bih content date       # Start date of the second agreement (4 October 2002)
  input date_of_failure content date         # Date of non-compliance
  input contribution_start_date content date # Start date of contribution
  input contribution_end_date content date   # End date of contribution
  output transition_period content date      # The date marking the transition
  output termination_date content date       # Date termination can occur
  output agreement_duration content duration # Duration of the agreement
```

## Personnel Coverage Transition

The personnel coverage transitions from the first agreement ending on 31 December 2002 to the second agreement starting on 4 October 2002.

```catala
scope AgreementTimeline:
  date round down
  definition transition_period equals end_date_planning_team
```

## Termination Notice Period

If a party fails to comply, the other party has the right to terminate the agreement by serving two months' notice.

```catala
scope AgreementTimeline:
  definition termination_date equals date_of_failure + 2 month
```

## Agreement Duration

The agreement remains in force for the duration of the contribution of the Republic of Latvia to the EUPM.

```catala
scope AgreementTimeline:
  definition agreement_duration equals contribution_end_date - contribution_start_date
```